<title>UK: BA opens lower on EU probe report.</title>
<headline>BA opens lower on EU probe report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Airways were marked lower in a rising market on Friday after a report the European Commission has launched a formal inquiry into BA's planned tie-up with American Airlines.</p>
<p>BA shares were down 1-1/2p at 589-1/2p by 0815 GMT while the broader market was indicated 0.28 percent higher.</p>
<p>The Times newspaper said the Commission wrote to the airlines, saying the proposed alliance did not appear to be in the interests of consumers and they have 60 days to respond.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
